# Wiki content (LLM)

If a lesson introduces a reusable **procedure**, **theorem**, **formula**, or **problem type**, also add a catalog object. Do **not** edit ScratchNotes, WikiDetail, or MDXComponents — `catalog.js` concatenates the kind files.

| Kind | File | Practice (auto from fields) |
| --- | --- | --- |
| procedure | `src/data/wiki/procedures.js` | rank steps (`order`) |
| theorem | `src/data/wiki/theorems.js` | rank deduction (`order`) |
| formula | `src/data/wiki/formulas.js` | chart (`explorer`) + type KaTeX (`tex` / `formula`) |
| problem | `src/data/wiki/problems.js` | guided from start (`sample`) |

Required: unique `id`, `title`, `href` to the lesson. `kind` is inferred if omitted.

- **order:** shuffle `items`; `order` is the correct index permutation (never list steps already in order). Include `prompt` and `why`.
- **formula:** `formula` + `tex` + `texAlts` (frac/dfrac, mid vs `|`). Optional `explorer` id in `formulaExplorer/presets.js`. Optional `order` is browse-only.
- **problem:** `sample` id registered in `guidedChoice/guides/index.js`. Practice hides the worked solution (`startMode=guided`, `hideReveal`).
- Do not dump every exercise into wiki — only the **type** (pattern + one sample).
- Original prose; do not paste copyrighted textbook listings. Opening a card is not study; first real interact → study; practice pass → learned.
- Practice already runs on the current list (random 25 / search / bookmarked / study / learned). Do not special-case pools.
